 "text": "A galaxy is at a distance of 60 million light-years from the Earth. The galaxy is moving away at a\nspeed of 1300km/s.\nOne light-year is about 9.5 × 1012\nkm.\nThere are about 3.2 × 107 seconds in one year.\nWhich expression can be used to estimate the age of the Universe in years?\n60 \u0002 106\u0002 3.2 \u0002 107\nA\n1300 \u0002 9.5 \u0002 1012\n60 \u0002 106\u0002 9.5 \u0002 1012\nB\n1300 \u0002 3.2 \u0002 107\n1300 \u0002 9.5 \u0002 1012\nC\n60 \u0002 106\u0002 3.2 \u0002 107\n1300 \u0002 3.2 \u0002 107\nD\n60 \u0002 106\u0002 9.5 \u0002 1012\nBLANK PAGE",
